WEBVTT

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:28.560
Yunocchi, morning!

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.880
Coming!

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.260
Good morning, Miya-chan!

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.840
Yunocchi, is that your sketchbook?

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:40.930
Yeah!

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.600
I brought it since we're drawing in class today.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.040
Good morning!

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:54.180
Yuno-san, Miyako-san, good morning!

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.660
Good morning!

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.570
Morning!

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:58.120
Good morning!

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.400
Hiro-san, you don't look well.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.160
Yeah, I didn't get much sleep.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.290
You still have bed hair.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.520
That part of my hair never settles down, okay!

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:13.420
Miyako-san, you still have bed hair too.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:14.170
Oh.

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.300
You sort of have it too, Nori-chan!

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:17.800
What?!

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:20.180
This is embarrassing.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.640
Hurry up. Class is about to start!

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.080
Okay!

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.200
Whistling a cheerful tune

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.200
youki ni kuchibue fuite

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.540
I join the birds chirping by the window

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.540
madobe no kotori to sesshon

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:53.460
When fatigue strikes

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:53.460
suima ga yatte kite

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.090
My imagination runs wild

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:56.090
atama ga danshingu

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:58.550
Everything in life makes me smile

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:58.550
nan demo kan demo waraeru nichijou

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.380
Nothing really new takes place

00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.380
okimari na kishoutenketsu

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.010
But sometimes it's exciting to spice things up

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.010
demo demo tama ni wa piritto supaisu

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:06.640
Let's paint it on the blue sky

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:06.640
aozora peintingu

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:07.680
Where should we go?

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:07.680
doko ikou

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.270
Let's stay here

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.270
koko ni iyou

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.270
What's that?

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.270
sore wa nani

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:11.850
I wanna try that!

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:11.850
are yaritai

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:14.440
Let's make this moment count

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:14.440
ima ni tokubetsu na shirushi

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.820
How fast my clock moves is all up to me

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.820
tokeibari no mawashikata watashi shidai kamo

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.490
With a rich palette of colors from the four seasons

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:23.490
shiki oriori iro toridori

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.950
Our laid-back everyday lives can be

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.950
nonbiri na everyday

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.580
Any blend of pastel, vivid, and metro colors

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.580
pasuteru bibiddo metoro

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.410
Anyone can create their own coloring

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.410
jibun dake no karaaringu

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:34.000
So when your heart races in excitement

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:34.000
sono tokidoki mune doki doki

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.710
Just draw a sun at the top

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.710
hachamecha na taiyou ni oegaki

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:41.840
And let your inner artist take you from there

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:41.840
tobidasu aatishizumu

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.180
Can I hold your hand tight?

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.180
gyutto shite ii kana

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.560
I've been sketching everything I love

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:52.560
suki suki suki wo sukecchi

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.100
And painting them in rainbow colors

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.100
nijiiro ni somete iku yo

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:59.860
All right, I'm off to have some more fun!

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:59.860
sore ja ittekimasu

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:03.030
September 25th

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:03.030
Chatter Sketch

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.830
Yunocchi, you're funny-looking.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.420
Don't look!

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.690
Are you having a hard time deciding what to draw?

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:22.650
Remember, they're objects you see all the time,

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.370
so you have to free yourself of preconceptions.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.180
The key is to look and observe!

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.870
I can draw myself <i>without</i> looking, though!

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:32.850
Unreal!

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:36.250
Sensei, do you think you could draw Mashiko-sensei too?

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.610
Mashiko-sensei?

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.430
Mashiko-sensei...

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:44.620
It sucks.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.200
I've been staring at it for so long that I'm getting Gestalt psychosis.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:50.960
Ges...?

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:52.960
Like I'm...

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.960
disintegrating!

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.670
Wh-What's going on?

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.880
Drawing hands comes up often on art college entrance exams, don't they?

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:04.890
Yeah.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.100
I practiced drawing hands a lot before the Yamabuki entrance exam.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.290
You did?

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:13.010
They don't cost money, for one thing.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:14.810
I drew tons of them!

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.090
I see!

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:19.610
When I wanted to draw a bottle, I went and bought a Ramune.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:21.860
That sounds like a lot of trouble.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:26.200
But I kept unconsciously breaking them to get to the marble inside.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.700
The marble?

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:29.450
Huh?

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:32.290
This was back when you were in middle school?

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:38.590
I think this is the first time you've ever mentioned how you prepared for the entrance exam.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:39.610
Is it?

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:40.300
Yeah!

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.510
We've talked about a whole bunch of things so far,

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.760
but I guess there are still things that haven't even come up!

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:47.550
Well, of course!

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.680
We have like 15 years' worth of stories to tell!

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.680
But no one remembers the first three years of their life.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:54.470
Huh?

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.270
You're right.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.270
I guess it's more like 12 years, then.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:01.280
You looked surprised just now.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:06.160
There are so many faces we haven't shown each other yet.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.160
Huh?

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:08.410
Are there?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:09.410
Sure there are!

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.530
For instance...

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.500
Yunocchi, try sneering.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:14.730
Sneer...

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:17.250
Like mocking somebody?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.670
Wow, that's so <i>not</i> it.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:22.250
What?!

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:29.130
I wonder how well I know you right now.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:34.100
Well, I'm not even sure how well I know myself, truth be told.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.330
The other day, I was on a train,

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:40.310
and there was this little girl standing near the door.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.320
Oh, and?

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:44.070
When I walked to the door to get off,

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:47.320
it turned out I was shorter than her!

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:48.320
Oh, wow.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.170
Then I realized just how short I am, which was a surprise.

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.660
It took you that long?

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.920
All right, that's it for the composition.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.920
Now it's time to start drawing!

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.920
I need to give each surface a rich palette of texture!

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:09.300
The palette of texture will give objects a sense of perspective!

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:10.800
Palette!

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:12.300
Palette!

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:16.150
Palate.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:21.810
All right!

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.150
And it's time!

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:28.070
We won't be critiquing them this time, so please just turn them in to me!

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:30.790
I'm done!

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.330
Oh, Yunocchi, that's a bold composition!

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.330
I went a little wild for this one.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.370
Miya-chan, yours is...

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.580
Oh, right!

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:43.340
She didn't say it had to be <i>your</i> hand.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:47.970
I just drew what I saw in the mirror.

00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.350
Yunocchi, my bad!

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:52.720
I was just kidding.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.330
I can tell it's a picture of you just by looking.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:59.200
It's cute, just like you!

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.730
C-Cu...

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:01.480
Huh?

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:04.190
Haven't I ever told you?

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.730
You're adorable, Yunocchi.

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:09.430
M-Miya-chan, you're way cuter!

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:10.490
You're beautiful!

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.550
What are you saying?

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:16.330
All right, I'll go turn in my drawing, then.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.210
Oh, okay.

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:18.870
I'll be turning mine in soon too.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:20.710
<i>Huh, Miyako-san?</i>

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.710
<i>I don't think I've ever seen her make that face.</i>

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:36.270
Hey, Miya-chan, do you want to sleep over in my room tonight?

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:36.810
Hm?

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.870
This might sound strange, since we talk plenty every day,

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:43.310
but I want to talk with you even more today.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:45.060
Oh, I'll be coming over, then!

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:46.070
Great!

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:51.070
Maybe I'll make a conversation die and bring it over.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:51.950
Sounds good!

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:54.970
But don't put "scary story" on one of the sides, okay?

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:56.450
Got it!

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:04.470
This reminds me...

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:09.840
The night I moved here, you came over to use the bath.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.090
Oh, I remember that.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:16.610
I was in the bath, then you suddenly opened the door and came inside.

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:20.980
I didn't know what kind of person you were yet, so I was so surprised.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.980
You've always been you, Miya-chan.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:27.950
Take that!

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:34.610
As I said,

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:39.620
curry tastes better when you let it sit for a day to bring out the flavor.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:43.400
But wouldn't you rather eat it right away?

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.550
I can't wait a whole day.

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:49.450
Come on. Why can't you wait?

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:52.550
I want fresh, piping-hot curry!

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:56.830
So you have to be patient

00:08:56.830 --> 00:09:02.370
and leave it for a while for the curry to have more flavor.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:11.070
September 25th

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:11.070
End

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:11.070
To Be Continued

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:21.570
<i>I've always liked working on details since I was little.</i>

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:23.930
Weather update.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:26.810
The high-pressure system in the Pacific...

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:29.590
<i>When I drew detailed pictures,</i>

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:31.710
<i>my parents and teachers complimented me.</i>

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.960
<i>That made me really happy, so I drew even more.</i>

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:42.430
<i>They agreed right away when I said I wanted to go to an art high school,</i>

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:45.680
<i>so I applied to Yamabuki High School.</i>

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.930
Today, from the east of Japan to the west, a vast...

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.690
Now what?

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.690
September 29th-30th, Hiro-san

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:00.700
What should I do?!

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.450
It's due tomorrow!

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:09.930
It's not like I have to go to a college to be able to write novels or draw pictures.

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:14.840
But I'm not popular enough to say I'll go pro instead of going to college.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.650
Maybe I should let God decide my fate!

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:24.090
Sae, calm down!

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.100
The individual counseling sessions are in a week.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.350
Sae!

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:33.310
Don't let it get you down.

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:34.610
Hiro!

00:10:35.020 --> 00:10:37.110
I want to eat something sweet.

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:37.860
What?

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:38.980
Jeez.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:40.230
All right.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:45.950
You'll be going to an art college, right?

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.710
Yeah, I suppose.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:50.210
That's where most of the class is going,

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.160
so I can't help but hesitate,

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:55.920
but I'm thinking of going with a humanities program.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:12.870
Hey, Miya-chan!

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:15.150
Could you eat the rest?

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:19.820
Hiro-san, didn't you say something like that last time too?

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.320
Huh, did I?

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.570
Yeah! I'll take you to the infirmary.

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:24.070
What?

00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:24.820
Oh, right.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.450
You're too heavy for me to carry,

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.450
so you'll have to walk.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:29.950
Miya-chan!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:36.050
And so Kuwahara-sensei, I'll let you handle the rest!

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:37.580
Got it! Thanks.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:42.170
You should lie down for a bit.

00:11:42.170 --> 00:11:43.970
But I'm not really...

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.430
You don't look well.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:50.230
<i>I don't look well, huh?</i>

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.560
Be gentle!

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:57.250
Wh-Why are you here?

00:11:57.250 --> 00:11:58.560
You see...

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:05.070
I thought I'd chat with Kuwahara-sensei during lunch break, but when I came here,

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:08.320
Kuwahara-sensei was occupied,

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:11.080
and I didn't see anyone resting on the bed,

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.580
so I sat down on the bed and waited.

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:14.580
But then...

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.510
The bed got bigger, sparkling in rainbow colors,

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:19.670
and swallowed me!

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:23.510
She fell fast asleep.

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:28.490
This is the infirmary, so keep it quiet.

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:34.810
So why are <i>you</i> here, Hiro-san?

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:38.310
I had no appetite, so wanted to rest a bit.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:40.690
Are you worried about something?

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:41.570
Huh?

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:43.010
I'm here to listen!

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:44.320
It can be anything. Just tell me!

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:45.320
What?!

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:48.110
Kuwahara-sensei, one katsudon, please!

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:49.570
That's for police interrogations!

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:54.110
I wouldn't say I'm <i>worried</i> about it,

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:56.970
but thinking about my future is just overwhelming.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:13:01.630
Oh, right, it's that time of the year when the third-years have to make the big decision.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:05.110
I'm thinking I should to go to an art college,

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:08.380
and then become an art teacher.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:11.890
Oh, great! You want to be a teacher?

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:17.570
It's a wonderful job where you get to show your students how fun art is!

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:19.850
Go for it!

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:21.610
Okay.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:27.360
And maybe I'll get to teach at Yamabuki like you.

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:31.690
Even if you become a teacher,

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:35.240
there's very little chance you'll be assigned to Yamabuki.

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:42.830
Well... I just can't imagine myself being anywhere else.

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:43.840
So...

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:49.050
Teachers have a big influence on the students.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:53.450
A single careless remark can demoralize everyone.

00:13:54.120 --> 00:13:57.590
Teachers interact with students when they're the most sensitive.

00:13:57.590 --> 00:14:01.020
Teachers, as you can see, play an important role.

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:05.770
Hiro-san, do you <i>really</i> want to become a teacher?

00:14:06.140 --> 00:14:08.280
Or do you just want to stay here?

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.150
Eh?

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:13.780
Even if you become a teacher and get assigned to Yamabuki,

00:14:13.780 --> 00:14:18.070
Sae-san and your current underclassmen won't be at Yamabuki.

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:19.150
Will you be fine with that?

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:35.500
<i>Sae-san and your current underclassmen won't be at Yamabuki.</i>

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:36.680
<i>Will you be fine with that?</i>

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.630
<i>She saw through me.</i>

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:42.440
<i>I just don't want to change.</i>

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.550
<i>I love drawing,</i>

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:52.150
<i>but I love living at Hidamari Apartments with Sae and everyone else even more.</i>

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:56.670
I don't want to graduate!

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:00.910
Kuwahara-sensei!

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:04.690
I think I said something too harsh.

00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:07.370
She should be able to handle it.

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:10.260
I hope I didn't sound too negative.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:11.690
I can't really say.

00:15:11.690 --> 00:15:14.630
You ended up talking about life beyond college.

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:19.490
It was sad that she was only looking back when talking about the future,

00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:21.520
so I had to say something.

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:26.410
I think you're a good teacher.

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:27.770
Really?

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:29.150
Yep!

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:30.530
Just sometimes, though.

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:36.530
Sae-san!

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.530
Yuno, Miyako!

00:15:38.530 --> 00:15:40.450
Huh? Where's Hiro-san?

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:42.910
Hiro left school early after fifth period.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:44.410
What?!

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:46.970
Is she that sick?

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:48.590
Should we go see her?

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:51.450
Should we make porridge for her?

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:55.090
We'll go check in on her later, so it'd be nice if you made some.

00:15:55.090 --> 00:15:56.840
Okay!

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.100
Yunocchi!

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:02.350
I'll help you make the porridge!

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:03.600
Thanks!

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:07.430
There isn't much to do since it's just rice porridge, though.

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:12.320
Oh, you could take out the seeds from pickled plums to make it easier for Hiro-san to eat.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:17.710
I guess I should let Nazuna and Nori know about Hiro-san's condition too.

00:16:17.710 --> 00:16:18.820
Yeah.

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:24.700
It's from Yuno-san.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:26.960
Hiro-san is...

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:30.450
Well, she didn't look so well this morning.

00:16:30.450 --> 00:16:32.960
Wh-What should we do?!

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:36.450
Nazuna, calm down.

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:37.530
But...

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:38.670
Listen.

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:41.330
Since Yuno-san sent us the message,

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:44.970
Sae-san and Miyako-san probably know about this already.

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:50.440
So let's think about what we can do for Hiro-san.

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:51.230
Yeah!

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:01.240
Nazuna!

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:02.490
What's up?

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.530
Um...

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:08.460
I heard from Yuno-san that Hiro-san's not doing well.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:11.330
Oh, yeah, she's not.

00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:12.130
Please...

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:14.170
give this to Hiro-san!

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:19.290
All right.

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:20.840
Thank you.

00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:23.690
Hiro was asleep when I stopped by earlier,

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:25.770
so I'll give this to her when I visit her tonight.

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:27.520
Okay!

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:35.070
Hiro-san!

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:36.290
It's pitch dark!

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:38.530
Looks like she's still sleeping.

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:46.590
Sae-san, I'll leave the porridge on the stove.

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:47.790
That'd be great.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:51.790
Then we'll leave the rest to you!

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:53.290
Okay.

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:05.810
Huh? I...

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:08.090
Oh, you're up, Hiro.

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:10.560
You were fast asleep, so I just came in.

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:12.150
Sae...

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:16.150
You left this on the chair, so I saw it.

00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:20.550
No, th-that's not it!

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:21.150
That's...

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:23.410
Becoming a teacher sounds great!

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:27.930
Hiro, you're great at explaining.

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:30.670
You explain things from the other person's perspective,

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:32.420
so it's easy to understand.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:37.770
You're kind, considerate, and open-minded.

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:40.050
I think you found a perfect dream for yourself.

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:42.550
Remember when I told you

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:47.720
I used to dislike drawing animals because of what an art teacher told me?

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:51.050
I wish I had you as a teacher.

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:58.070
Why are you crying?

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:06.570
Sae, thank you.

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:07.420
Huh?

00:19:07.420 --> 00:19:09.050
Y-Yeah.

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:14.020
I'm sad that I'll have to graduate.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:18.840
It means I'll leave Hidamari Apartments and won't get to see you as often.

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:26.610
I'm sad too, of course.

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:28.100
I really am.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:30.780
But you know what? It'll be all right.

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:31.770
We'll be the same.

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:39.900
As long as we wish for it, everything will be okay.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:43.150
I'm sure it'll be even better than things are now.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:44.430
Okay.

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:51.590
Jeez!

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.650
You haven't eaten much recently, after all.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:58.550
It just happened when I felt so relieved.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:02.670
Oh, Yuno and Miyako made some rice porridge for you.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:04.980
How nice of them!

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:05.680
Huh?

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.490
It's from Nori-chan!

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:10.180
Hm?

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:20.640
Yeah, everyone was worried about you when they heard you left school early.

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:22.070
This is from Nazuna.

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:34.470
Morning, everyone!

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:36.160
Good morning!

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:38.540
Are you feeling better, Hiro-san?

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:40.350
Yeah, I'm all right now!

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:41.540
Thanks for the porridge.

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:45.170
Me, me! I took the seeds out of the pickled plums!

00:20:45.170 --> 00:20:47.510
It was very delicious!

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:50.300
Your cooling pad helped me too, Nazuna-chan!

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:51.810
That's a relief!

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:54.060
And thanks for the text, Nori-chan!

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:55.430
Oh, no problem.

00:20:55.430 --> 00:20:56.710
Morning.

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:58.690
Good morning!

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:02.150
Morning, Sae!

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:02.940
Morning.

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:03.940
Hiro-san!

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:07.110
Today's lunch special is foie gras bowl!

00:21:07.110 --> 00:21:08.730
What? Is it?

00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:12.090
Hiro-san, would it be okay to eat that when you've just recovered?

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:14.390
Stock is limited, so we've got to hurry!

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:18.310
Is it? Then we'll have to get it before it's sold out!

00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:21.030
I can tell the cafeteria will get chaotic.

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:23.130
I'll get it, no matter what!

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.550
That enthusiasm!

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:26.970
That's the Hiro-san I know!

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:27.970
Jeez!

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:31.220
Are you saying I'm just a glutton?

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:39.920
Yoshinoya-sensei, good morning!

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:41.900
Hiro-san, good morning!

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:44.530
Sorry about yesterday.

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:46.530
I suddenly stopped responding and cut the conversation.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:48.010
Oh, don't worry about that!

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:50.780
I probably sounded too mean. I'm so sorry!

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:54.990
I'll apply to art colleges to become an art teacher!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:59.090
Oh, did you make up your mind?

00:21:59.090 --> 00:21:59.790
I did!

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:05.300
Someone who knows me better than I do reassured me.

00:22:10.640 --> 00:22:12.840
Let's turn "Hidamari Apartments" into English!

00:22:12.840 --> 00:22:14.620
Sunshine-something Apartments?

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:16.660
That's already complicated!

00:22:16.660 --> 00:22:18.540
It means the apartments are a sunny place, so...

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:19.320
I got it!

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:21.000
"Sun-rich Soy Sauce House"!

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:22.140
How did you come up with <i>that</i>?

00:22:22.140 --> 00:22:25.180
It means the place where there's rich exposure to the sun!

00:22:25.180 --> 00:22:27.820
Then, wouldn't just "Sunny Place House" work?

00:22:27.820 --> 00:22:30.080
Hiro-san, bravo!

00:22:30.080 --> 00:22:33.520
Next time: "October 5th-6th, Pamphlet Compepe."

00:22:33.520 --> 00:22:36.180
"October 6th-8th, A Secret Date."

00:22:36.180 --> 00:22:39.920
We'll be waiting at Yamabuki High School, so come visit us!
